{:edb/db-before-t 663 :edb/db-after-t 664 :edb/tx-data [[13194139533976 50 #inst "2026-10-05T23:11:26.300Z" 13194139533976 true] [17592186096763 1020 #edb/ref 17592186275544 13194139533976 true] [17592186096763 1020 #edb/ref 17592186275551 13194139533976 true] [17592186096764 1020 #edb/ref 17592186275537 13194139533976 true] [17592186096764 1020 #edb/ref 17592186275555 13194139533976 true] [17592186096764 1020 #edb/ref 17592186275558 13194139533976 true] [17592186275537 1017 #edb/ref 17592186275538 13194139533976 true] [17592186275537 1089 "q-2401" 13194139533976 true] [17592186275537 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533976 true] [17592186275537 1100 "Find ${y}^{′}$ for $y=4{x}^{2}\\sqrt{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}.$" 13194139533976 true] [17592186275537 1113 #uuid "b6953033-5b86-5efc-a511-cf9d2c38992f" 13194139533976 true] [17592186275537 1145 "This question requires the product rule. Let $u(x)=4{x}^{2}$ and $v(x)=\\sqrt{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}.$ Then\n\n$$\n{u}^{′}(x)=8x,\\,{v}^{′}(x)=\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{2\\sqrt{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}}.\n$$\n\nNote that we used the chain rule to differentiate $v.$\n\nNow, applying the product rule and simplifying, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}=\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={u}^{′}(x)\\cdot v(x)+u(x)\\cdot {v}^{′}(x) \\\\  & =(8x)(\\sqrt{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x})+(4{x}^{2})(\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{2\\sqrt{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}}) \\\\  & =8x\\sqrt{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}+\\frac{2{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\sqrt{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}} \\\\  & =\\frac{8x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+2{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\sqrt{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533976 true] [17592186275538 1000 #edb/ref 17592186275539 13194139533976 true] [17592186275538 1000 #edb/ref 17592186275540 13194139533976 true] [17592186275538 1000 #edb/ref 17592186275541 13194139533976 true] [17592186275538 1000 #edb/ref 17592186275542 13194139533976 true] [17592186275538 1000 #edb/ref 17592186275543 13194139533976 true] [1759